  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Calc",
      "h2": "Calculating pH of a weak acid",
      "body_html": "<p>Approximation: [H+]^2 / [HA] = Ka. So [H+] = sqrt(Ka × [HA]).</p><p>Equivalently: pH = 1/2 (pKa - log[HA]). Valid when [HA] >> [H+].</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Worked",
      "h2": "Worked example",
      "body_html": "<p>Ethanoic acid pKa = 4.76, [HA] = 0.10 mol/dm3.</p><p>pH = 1/2 (4.76 - log 0.10) = 1/2 (4.76 + 1) = 2.88.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Compare",
      "h2": "Comparing strengths",
      "body_html": "<p>Smaller pKa -> stronger acid (more dissociation). HCl pKa ≈ -7 (very strong). Ethanoic acid pKa 4.76 (weak).</p><p>Carbonic acid pKa1 ≈ 6.4. Phenol pKa ≈ 10. Water pKa ≈ 14.</p>"
    }
  ],
